=== PART B: a node signing a call to raise ITS OWN score is aborted on-chain ===
    rpi3, using its own key and its own AdminCap, targets its own address.

$ [rpi3] sui client call --package $PKG_V8 --module trust --function increase_guarded --args 0x38e59f73d7d2afdb2f59ebb85295d2d420771bcd102a5e8a7b599d2a7c034363 0xc38f75e77c01fdf8d8ce6162b6107d9e630fb61d46045f78156a31531b4eeb39 0x27dacda1bdcb3fb8dc2a4b0d77b420deea5bb43d1047592ddadb19f35764ea10 5 0x6
    -> MoveAbort code 4   digest=AQgvoUawC1NM2X4Qvgu23BYRqUtf8Un3sH1voYbEFxWH
    [PASS] rpi3 self-raise rejected (E_SELF_SCORING) (expected abort:4)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS SHOWS: no adversary-published module can reach the unguarded primitive
(Part A), and the guarded path aborts when the signer is the node being scored
(Part B, code 4). The aborted transaction is on-chain under the digest above.
